                <!-- INTERVIEW QUESTIONS -->

                <h3 class="fw-bold text-dark mt-5 mb-4">
                    Interview Questions
                </h3>

                <h5 class="fw-bold">
                    1. What is a Lambda Expression?
                </h5>

                <p class="text-muted mb-4">
                    A lambda expression is a concise way to represent an anonymous
                    function in C#.
                </p>

                <h5 class="fw-bold">
                    2. Which operator is used in a lambda expression?
                </h5>

                <p class="text-muted mb-4">
                    The <strong>=&gt;</strong> operator is used in lambda expressions.
                </p>

                <h5 class="fw-bold">
                    3. What is the difference between Action and Func?
                </h5>

                <p class="text-muted mb-4">
                    Action represents a delegate that returns no value, while Func
                    represents a delegate that returns a value.
                </p>

                <h5 class="fw-bold">
                    4. Where are lambda expressions commonly used?
                </h5>

                <p class="text-muted mb-4">
                    Lambda expressions are commonly used with LINQ, collections,
                    delegates, events, filtering, sorting, and data processing.
                </p>

                <h5 class="fw-bold">
                    5. Can a lambda expression have multiple statements?
                </h5>

                <p class="text-muted">
                    Yes. Multiple statements can be written inside curly braces,
                    and a return statement can be used when a value is required.
                </p>

